        "original_id": "a417ce68-9981-5dee-904e-a6ac7946e527",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnston Forbes-Robertson, Prince Hamlet, Gertrude Elliott, Claudius, King Hamlet, Maxine Elliott\n- Roles: Hamlet, Prince of Denmark, King of Denmark, stage actress\n- Topics: Victorian-era acting, theatre families\n\nFacts:\n- Prince Hamlet is the Prince of Denmark, the son of the previous King of Denmark, King Hamlet, and the nephew of the usurping Claudius.\n- Johnston Forbes-Robertson was considered the finest Hamlet of the Victorian era and one of the finest actors of his time.\n- Johnston Forbes-Robertson disliked acting and believed throughout his life that he was temperamentally unsuited to the profession.\n- Gertrude Elliott was born on December 14, 1874, and died on December 24, 1950.\n- Gertrude Elliott, later Lady Forbes-Robertson, was an American stage actress.\n- Gertrude Elliott belonged to an extended family of theatre professionals that included her husband Johnston Forbes-Robertson and her sister Maxine Elliott.",
